# The repository stores text as LF and checks it out as LF on every platform.
# This overrides `core.autocrlf`, which Git for Windows enables by default and
# which would otherwise rewrite the working tree to CRLF on checkout. That
# matters here beyond taste: the working tree is the Docker build context, and
# CRLF reaches the image in the nginx configuration and the Dockerfile itself.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, so Git never tries to normalise or diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Encoded certificates and keys are not text to be normalised either, in case a
# sample ever gets committed on purpose.
*.der binary
*.p12 binary
*.pfx binary
*.p7b binary

